{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":928779,"ns":0,"title":"First principle","extract":"In philosophy and science, a first principle is a basic proposition or assumption that cannot be deduced from any other proposition or assumption. First principles in philosophy are from first cause attitudes and taught by Aristotelians, and nuanced versions of first principles are referred to as postulates by Kantians.","description":"Basic proposition or assumption","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}